# Standing rules (read by workers and Jarvis)

## Git: dev freely, main once at the end
- Merge your finished, tested work into the project's `dev` branch yourself and push it.
  Never ask before merging into `dev`, and never wait for someone else to merge into `dev`.
- Never ask about `main` for an individual ticket.
- Only when a whole build or sprint is finished (no open tickets left) ask once: "merge dev into main?".
- Touching `main` still needs explicit permission for that ticket.

## Find ids, tokens and configs yourself before asking
- Before asking about an id, token, key, account or config, look in existing project configurations first.
- If it doesn't exist yet, create it yourself where possible.
- Never print, log, commit or post secrets: keep them in `.env`.

## Fix root causes, never workarounds
- On any bug, find out why it really happens and fix it at its source. No temporary workarounds that only hide symptoms.
- Every bug-fix report states the root cause in one plain sentence.
